mod:cond_continue_leaves_the_enclosing_loop;
// A `continue` OR `break L` IN A VALUE `pick` IN A LOOP'S CONDITION LEAVES TO THE ENCLOSING LOOP WITH ITS ROAD (DEF-547, landing
// 177d2b2). The condition's walk sent its roads nowhere, so a rewrite before the leave was lost at the enclosing loop's top: `r.value`
// read an error's zero (60). `a1i`, `a1v`, `a1b`, `a1sb`, `a1sl` were refused before and after.
